{# Storewide section-heading style (ThemeSettings.heading_align/size/font) —
   NOT for merchant banner text (hero/promo/category/product), which has its
   own text_hidden/hide_cta/hide_overlay controls.

   `default_size` and `default_align` are that heading's own original
   Tailwind classes — used as-is when heading_size is "md" / heading_align is
   blank (every store's default), so an untouched store looks exactly as it
   did before this existed. Some headings (testimonials, "Why it works") are
   center-aligned by the skin's own design, not by any single default this
   macro could otherwise safely pick. #}
{% macro heading_classes(default_size='text-2xl sm:text-3xl', default_align='text-left') %}{{
  'font-sans' if heading_font == 'sans' else 'font-display'
}} {{
  {'left': 'text-left', 'center': 'text-center', 'right': 'text-right'}[heading_align] if heading_align else default_align
}} {{
  {'sm': 'text-xl sm:text-2xl', 'md': default_size,
   'lg': 'text-3xl sm:text-4xl', 'xl': 'text-4xl sm:text-5xl'}[heading_size or 'md']
}}{% endmacro %}

{# A heading that shares its row with a "View all" / "All products" link sits
   in a flex row — as a flex item it shrinks to its own text width, so
   heading_classes()'s text-center/text-right has nothing to visibly center
   or push against. This picks the row's justify-* to match, so the heading
   (grouped with its link) actually moves as heading_align says. Pass the
   row's own default justify class (almost always "justify-between") so an
   untouched store's layout is byte-for-byte unchanged. #}
{% macro heading_row_class(default='justify-between') %}{{
  {'left': default, 'center': 'justify-center', 'right': 'justify-end'}[heading_align] if heading_align else default
}}{% endmacro %}
